---
description: Rules for editing any JavaScript file in engine/ or data/
globs: engine/**/*.js,data/**/*.js
alwaysApply: false
---

- Every file starts with `'use strict';` and is a classic script, not a module. No `import`, `export`, `require`.
- Top-level names are global. Search the repo before adding one; a clash is silent. Put new code in a file-local IIFE `(function(){ ... })();` like the move files do.
- A file can only use names defined in files above it in `index.html` at load time. New files must be added to `index.html` at the right spot.
- Some files wrap earlier functions (see `engine/dialog-voice.js`). Do not reorder `<script>` tags without checking.
- Do not change the shape of saved state without a migration (`migrateSave` in `engine/story.js`).
- Do not hand-edit or reformat big data files (sprites, maps, scenes) beyond the lines you are changing. Search for the section; do not open the whole file.
